  ── If the spreads are unequal ──────────────
  Welch's F does not pool the within-group spread, and Games-Howell
  uses each pair's own spread instead of one shared error term. Where
  these agree with the block above, the unequal spread did not change
  the conclusion. Where they disagree, prefer these -- that is what
  they are for.

  Welch's F           F(2, 25.74) = 5.4117
